    // bounded by a `count` parameter (u8[1 10]) and making a slice from it. It
    // asserts the analyzer publishes the bounded-region fact (NonNull, alignment 4,
    // element-count reference `arg_count` over [1, 10]) onto the pointer, its alias,
    // and the produced slice (length [1, 10]). There is no embedded Stark source; a
    // plausible equivalent that builds a bounded slice from a count-bounded raw
    // pointer is reconstructed here. The structured bounded-region/nullability/
    // alignment facts are not reachable through the text bridge, so this is reduced
